obs ERRATUM, added on recovery 20260906.070005 -- this lap died between its work and its send. fleet_round_open.sh stashed it whole at 20260906.062531, a later petrichor lap read the stash back under %464's discipline, and none of it had reached HEAD. Then the fetch before that send found de5fe7068, in which a peer had landed the SAME finding an hour earlier and gone further: the same two file names, 18 pen behaviors against this lap's 12, SIX living surfaces repaired against this lap's three, the jail_nesting capability red this lap named and left, a roster row for standing_equipment beside the one for compass_rose, and rows %467 and %468 folded to their own shelf on the lap that wrote them -- a better answer to the full pin than sizing a row down to it. So the recovering lap DROPPED everything here that overlapped and kept only what was additive: construction/README.md, which is the seventh living surface and is in neither the peer's six nor their row, and three more living pages this reading found -- construction/EQUINOX_SEAT_MAP.md, docs/PROVEN_SEAT.md, and context/rankings.kyri, whose 27-slot rota tended two pointer stubs at ranks 21 and 22. The scan and control described below are the peer's now, and theirs are better. This record stands because the duplication is itself the measurement: two ships spent one lap each on one finding, an hour apart, with nothing in the ledger to say the red was being worked -- which is exactly the open question the card has been carrying.
scope one red booked and repaired, one guard given the ability to see what it was guarding, one front door molted
status GREEN -- compass_rose 12/12 in the pen and green on metal, replay reds on real history, standing_equipment my row parses clean, living_pin_near_bound green, reds_ledger_headline green
recommend keep-going -- the scan meters the rose alone, and construction/README.md carried the same class of claim six times with nothing watching it; the near door is whether a page's claim about a live card is worth metering generally, which is one sentence of Keaton's and sized in the row.
